Z||000000||watts||10-26-2001||02:31 AM||||Ok - this is going to sound really lame, but...  I'll ask anyhow.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm just reassembling my '88 2.8, and I made a slight error.  I forgot to note the exact position of a few bolts.  Namely, the water pump, and the pan.<P>On the pump, these are a whack of bolts, but only 4 really large ones.  2 of those large ones are sort of a stud like affair.  If you numbered the large holes 1 to 4 from the top left across then the bottom left across, which holes would have the studs?<P>Also, on the pan, there are 4 studs.  Which holes had the studs, and are they really needed?  I can't remember anything attached to the posts.<P>Damn me for not taking more 'before' pictures.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Thanks for the help as usual.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||watts||10-26-2001||05:15 PM||||nobody????<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||10-26-2001||08:49 PM||||the studs go in the second and third holes from the right of the pully on the top. These hold a small bracket which is to deflect the A/C belt if it snaps as well as holding the bracket for the oil sending unit.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
